# Task: Route a syslog facility to a dedicated log file

An application on this server logs through the syslog facility `{{facility}}`, and its messages must be collected in a dedicated file.

1. Create the rsyslog configuration file `{{conf_file}}` with a rule that routes all messages of facility `{{facility}}` (any priority) to the file `{{log_file}}`.
2. Restart the rsyslog service so the rule is active.
3. Send a test syslog message through facility `{{facility}}` whose text contains exactly the token `{{test_token}}`, and confirm it was written to `{{log_file}}`.

The configuration must persist across reboots.
